<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 20 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 20 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said it</p>
<p>has qualified for bond insurance the following 20 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>    ---Belleville Comm. No.522, Ill., $3.9 million general</p>
<p>obligation bonds.</p>
<p>    --Niles Public Library District, Ill., $3.875 million</p>
<p>library GOs.</p>
<p>    --Malden, Mass., $4.4 million muni purpose loan GOs.</p>
<p>    --Maryland Depart of Transportation, Md., $50 million</p>
<p>revenue bonds.</p>
<p>    --Duluth, Minn., $1.960 million GO equipment certificates</p>
<p>and $1.285 million GOs.</p>
<p>    --Nevada, $45.130 million GOs.</p>
<p>    --Mount Pleasant, N.Y., $2.250 million, $1.103 million and</p>
<p>$1.537 million public improvement GOs.</p>
<p>    --Sachem CSD, N.Y., school district bonds $7.2 million.</p>
<p>    --Portland, Oregon, $110 million sewer system revenue</p>
<p>bonds.</p>
<p>    --Grove City Area SD, Pa., $5 million GOs and $5 million</p>
<p>GOs under the alternate bidding program.</p>
<p>    --Cumberland, R.I., $2 million GOs.</p>
<p>    --Lower Colorado River Authority, Texas, $1 million</p>
<p>refunding revenue bonds and $204.170 million refunding revenue</p>
<p>bonds.</p>
<p>    --Orange County Water, Texas, $3.045 million GOs.</p>
<p>    --Vermont, $38 million GOs.</p>
<p>    --Jackson County School District, Miss., $4.250 million</p>
<p>and $9.550 million.</p>
<p>    --U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650  REUTER (c) Reuters Limited 1996</p>
</text>
